Z||000000||ezsurf||03-27-2000||02:25 PM||||I'm looking for a stock replacement exhaust system for my 86SE.  The Fiero store has a cat back system by gorlic for $179, but I haven't found anything by anyone else.  The Fiero store does have some hard to find parts, but they don't always have the best deals.  Has anyone found anything else?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMeister||03-27-2000||03:23 PM||||I have a complete exhaust system in great shape off of an '86 SE V6.  It's for sale for $100.  Hope this helps.||||reg||6
Z||000002||ezsurf||03-27-2000||04:43 PM||||I'd like to know how many miles you have on the system, and exactly what components are you refering to when you say "complete exhaust system"?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||03-27-2000||08:44 PM||||Whatz up EZ, I think Wrenchead.com has a walker muffler, not sure if it's the complete system?||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroMeister||03-28-2000||11:16 AM||||The complete exhaust system that I have is everything past the y-pipe.  Does not include the y-pipe.  It's the down pipe, the cat (not sure of condition), piping to muffler, muffler (not sure of condition), the dual exhaust to the quad tips and the quad tips.  Hope this helps.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||ezsurf||03-28-2000||11:49 AM||||FieroMeister,<BR>What you described is basically what I have right now.  I don't know how old my current system is, but it has some miles on it.  It doesn't have any leaks or anything.  But, since I just rebuilt the engine, I'm thinking of just replacing it with a new system and forgeting about it.  That way I don't have to go back under the hood and replace the whole thing in another 5000 miles.  If my system was trashed, I'd take your offer in a heartbeat, thanks anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroMeister||03-28-2000||07:13 PM||||EZ, no problem.  I understand completely.  Sounds like you already have what you need. At the most you should just replace the cat and muffler and stick with what you've got.  The Fiero systems are nice with very little back pressure.  If I'm not mistaken most of the system is made of a low grade of stainless steel which does deteriorate a little over time but will last a long time.  If I am mistaken I'm sure someone will point that out to both of us quickly.  Herb Adams used to race the Fieros in stock classes by just removing the muffler and running with only the cat.  He stated that the system was more than quiet enough with just the cat and that the back pressure was reduced a little.  Hope this helps.||||reg||6
